  "notes": "KANJI: Also written as {喩|たと}える or {譬|たと}える, though {例|たと}える is most common.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AをBに{例|たと}える: to compare A to B, to liken A to B\n- {何|なに}に{例|たと}えたらいいか: what could one compare it to\n\nRELATED: The noun form {例|たと}え means \"simile, metaphor, parable.\" The conjunction {例|たと}え...ても means \"even if\" and is a separate word.",
